  "title": "Step Pyramid of Djoser, Saqqara",
  "summary": "The Step Pyramid at Saqqara, built for King Djoser (Netjerykhet) of the Third Dynasty by his vizier Imhotep, rises in six stacked stages above the Memphite necropolis. It is the oldest known Egyptian stone monument and the first pyramid, replacing the earlier flat-topped mastaba tomb.",
